{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>You shall not surrender a slave.</b> When you go out to war, it is possible that a slave who is not Israelite will flee to their camp." "<b>From his master.</b> He too is not an Israelite, for it concerns the honor of HaShem, who is called upon Israel. And if an Israelite surrenders the slave to his master, this is a profanation of the Name; therefore you shall not wrong him."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:24:29.424110190Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}